-- EXPECT-LINES: 17 17 22
-- EXPECT-SOUND: 4
-- An unclosed bracket, and the file after it.
--
-- Layout is SUSPENDED inside brackets (L2), so without a second witness a
-- stray `(` swallows the rest of the file into one logical line and the batch
-- collapses to a single fault. Indentation is that witness: a line STARTING AN
-- ITEM at or left of the block column current when the bracket opened cannot
-- be inside it (L7). The filter reports at the OPENING `(`, force-closes, and
-- resumes.
--
-- What this pins beyond the existing L7 coverage: the batch keeps going. The
-- damaged `h` two declarations later is still found, so an abandoned bracket
-- costs its own declaration and does not end the run.
module M

f = (a + b

g : U64
g = 1

h y := 2

k = 3
